src-02-and-the-emmc
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.000
2026-11-03 the author, pointing to boxedPINE wiki/sources/parts/SRC-02a and SRC-02b (XOR Gate Transistor Circuits, a DeepSeek conversation of 2026-10-04), then to boxed omi-files/omi-tetragrammatron/dev-docs/archive, OMI eMMC Target as Tetrahedral Centroid Memory Model and OMI eMMC Boot Target Example: "this is old but t shows where the idea came from". The archive documents: eMMC as a carrier, not authority; its four regions BOOT0, BOOT1, SECURE and USER as the four faces of a tetrahedron, "the centroid is the memory unit where these four faces meet as a single relation"; the first flashable object a 512-bit boot envelope, a 256-bit prefix half (gauge, orientation) and a 256-bit bootstrap half. SRC-02 carries it: the centroid as BOOT0 XOR BOOT1 XOR SECURE XOR USER, and the delta law as the swaps XORed, Delta(x, c) = sigma16(x) XOR sigma32(x) XOR sigma64(x) XOR c, with a table for x 0 to 15 "verified 15/15" (swap-permutators); the record's eMMC (I-94, the proof tree I-190) descends from it. Checked, the table against the swaps: it is linear (each entry the XOR of its bits' columns), and its entries 0x00 to 0x07 are exactly the zpoly swaps (adjacent pairs, each nibble reversed, the byte reversed; polytope-cas), but from 0x08 on each differs from them by 0x81, its column for bit 3 0x94 where those swaps give 0x15; the swap functions SRC-02a writes out (swap16 the nibble swap, swap32 the 2-bit groups reversed, swap64 b XOR 0x04) give neither (0x04 at 0). So SRC-02's own code and its own table disagree, and the table is the zpoly delta but for one column. SRC-02b notes the centroid's 0x04 as asserted without derivation.

