blackboard-half
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.000
2026-11-03 the author, of the 2 MiB image's free half: "that other half is like the blackboard swap space, its like the cache, becuase the 256 is only needed for the 65536 resolution but the 512 allows for trying on new bits". In the record: 256 x 256 = 65,536, a wall of the normalised cube (normalised-space), and the proof Blob at the image's start is 8,192 bytes, 65,536 bits (I-94); the image's sectors are 512 bytes, the proof tree laid out one record a sector boundary (proof-emmc.ts); at 2 MiB the 137 records end at 1,055,744 bytes, so 1,041,408 bytes, about half, are not yet written. That free half as a blackboard, a swap space or cache where new bits are tried before they are kept, the 256 for the 65,536 and the 512 for the trying: the author's reading, not built (nothing yet writes there).

two-views
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.000
2026-11-03 the author, of blackboard-half: "its like how the dominoes have a horizontal and vertical view". In the record: Unicode's dominoes in two orientations, 49 horizontal and 49 vertical, the same values drawn turned a quarter (domino-fano, domino-plane); their 8 empty dots the vertical 4 and the horizontal 4, the cube's two colours, dark and light (domino-stella), the turning moves D, TD, WD taking one view to the other and the kept line T W TW keeping each. So the image's two halves, the kept record and the blackboard for trying new bits, as the dominoes' two views of the same values: the author's reading.

thirty-to-sixty
00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.000
2026-11-03 the author, of two-views: "yes of the same but when they are the circulation of the animation frame how the step.svg resolves 30 to 60". In the record, the author's own words of 2026-10-13 in proofs/svg/tools/e8.mjs: "the sum-30 is the sub cycle of the 60", "the 30 is either side and the 60 is both"; E8 in two frames, the even-parity sign bytes and the odd (frames.svg, 128 and 128), each frame its own Coxeter element c, c^30 = 1 and c^15 = -1, its 240 roots in 8 cycles of 30 (coxeter-plane.svg draws both); the step's 30 frames, 15 of c + r and 15 of c - r (instantiation-portal). So one frame circulates 30 and the two together, either side and both, 60: the two views of two-views as the two frames, the author's reading.
